# team/architecture — the object-free default read path

The default `execute()`/`fetchall()` path for a read-only SELECT now returns a
`ResultSet` over the columnar frame instead of a list of tuples: each batch is
copied out of /dev/shm one memcpy per column, the ring is released immediately,
and a tuple is built only for a row that is indexed or iterated. `stream()` and
the tuple-materialising escape hatch are unchanged.

## Commands

Build (change):

    flock /tmp/fpq-bench.lock -c 'docker build -q --target dev -t fpq-architecture -f docker/Dockerfile .'

Baseline and change, same command, one at a time, under the lock:

    flock /tmp/fpq-bench.lock -c 'docker run --rm --shm-size=3g -e BENCH_GIT_REV=baseline fpq-baseline benchmarks.sh 100000'
    flock /tmp/fpq-bench.lock -c 'docker run --rm --shm-size=3g -e BENCH_GIT_REV=architecture fpq-architecture benchmarks.sh 100000'
    flock /tmp/fpq-bench.lock -c 'docker run --rm --shm-size=3g -e BENCH_GIT_REV=baseline fpq-baseline benchmarks.sh 1000000'
    flock /tmp/fpq-bench.lock -c 'docker run --rm --shm-size=3g -e BENCH_GIT_REV=architecture fpq-architecture benchmarks.sh 1000000'

The 100K change run is the repeat of an earlier identical run whose PATHS
`stream()` cell read 6.59M against a reported spread of ±4.8%; the repeat read
8.53M and its DBAPI/core cells agreed with the first (7.28/7.41 vs 7.23/7.10),
so the repeat is the one recorded below.

